#question(title: [#set text(size: 13pt)
True or False - convergence, monotonicity,
and boundedness])[
  #set text(size: 13pt)

  + If a sequence is convergent, then it is
    bounded above.
  + If a sequence is bounded, then it is
    convergent
  + If a sequence is convergent, then it is
    eventually monotonic.
  + If a sequence is positive and converges
    to 0, then it is eventually monotonic.
  + If a sequence diverges to $oo$, then it
    is eventually monotonic.
  + If a sequence diverges, then it is
    unbounded.
  + If a sequence diverges and is unbounded
    above, then it diverges to $oo$.
  + If a sequence is eventually monotonic,
    then it is either convergent, divergent
    to $oo$, or divergent to $-oo$.
]
